              "excerptSha256": "1ec2f051acd0348735439144264d836c2c9b7940ee53f8ec1635fd50a7f6ca0b"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-toolkit-map",
        "moduleId": "probabilistic-model",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "note",
        "title": "本点工具地图",
        "markdown": "可以把本点看成一张工具箱地图：概率空间与事件回答“随机实验怎么描述”；随机变量与分布把实验结果映射成数；期望与方差刻画平均水平和波动；并的界、马尔科夫不等式、切比雪夫不等式与切诺夫界则把“坏事件发生的概率有多小”转化为可计算的上界。后续分析随机快速排序时，最常用的两条主线是期望的线性性质和尾概率界。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "textbook-chapter-context"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "textbook-probability-space",
        "moduleId": "probabilistic-model",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "有限概率空间与事件",
        "markdown": "在有限概率空间中，基本事件有穷个，每个基本事件的概率是 $[0,1]$ 中的数，且所有基本事件的概率之和等于 1。例如抛一枚均匀硬币，基本事件是正面向上和反面向上，概率各为 $1/2$。若干基本事件的组合称为事件，事件发生的概率等于其中基本事件的概率之和；例如掷一枚均匀的六面骰子，“得到偶数”这一事件由 2、4、6 三个基本事件组成，概率为 $1/6+1/6+1/6=1/2$。事件 $A$ 的概率记作 $\\Pr[A]$。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-1806e31d4fe9355410d41c62",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000168"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "第 11 章",
                "概率论预备知识"
              ],
              "lineStart": 9922,
              "lineEnd": 10003,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "9a0c45dc11fcad1719b50763f92c6e5e8671d5d5871170e328344fc4551433bf"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "textbook-union-bound",
        "moduleId": "probabilistic-model",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "formula",
        "title": "并的界",
        "markdown": "设 $A_1,A_2,\\dots,A_n$ 都是事件，$\\Pr[A_i]$ 为事件 $A_i$ 的概率，则\n\n$$\\Pr\\Big[\\bigcup_{i=1}^{n}A_i\\Big]\\le\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\Pr[A_i]$$\n\n这个不等式称为并的界。它把“至少发生一个事件”的概率上界化为各事件概率之和。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-1806e31d4fe9355410d41c62",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000168"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "第 11 章",
                "概率论预备知识"
              ],
              "lineStart": 9922,
              "lineEnd": 10003,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "9a0c45dc11fcad1719b50763f92c6e5e8671d5d5871170e328344fc4551433bf"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-union-bound-loose",
        "moduleId": "probabilistic-model",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "并的界只是一个上界",
        "markdown": "取三个事件 $A_1,A_2,A_3$，若每个事件的概率都是 $0.1$，并的界只告诉我们 $\\Pr[A_1\\cup A_2\\cup A_3]\\le 0.3$。真实概率可能远小于 $0.3$，因为这些事件可能大量重叠。使用并的界时应把结论理解为上界，而不是精确值或等号。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "textbook-union-bound"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "textbook-random-variable",
        "moduleId": "random-variables",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "随机变量与二项分布",
        "markdown": "随机变量是从概率空间到实数的映射，随机变量取各种值的概率就是它的分布。例如抛一枚均匀硬币 $n$ 次，记录正面向上的次数，就得到一个随机变量 $X$，取值范围是 $0,1,2,\\dots,n$，其分布为\n\n$$\\Pr[X=i]=\\binom{n}{i}2^{-n}$$\n\n这称为二项分布。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-1806e31d4fe9355410d41c62",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000168"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "第 11 章",
                "概率论预备知识"
              ],
              "lineStart": 9922,
              "lineEnd": 10003,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "9a0c45dc11fcad1719b50763f92c6e5e8671d5d5871170e328344fc4551433bf"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "textbook-binomial-estimate",
        "moduleId": "random-variables",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "formula",
        "title": "二项式系数的估计",
        "markdown": "在涉及二项分布的计算中，常用下面的二项式系数估计：对 $1\\le k\\le n$，\n\n$$\\Big(\\frac{n}{k}\\Big)^{k}\\le\\binom{n}{k}\\le\\Big(\\frac{en}{k}\\Big)^{k}$$\n\n它把组合数夹在两个只含幂运算的量之间，便于在渐近分析中处理阶乘。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-1806e31d4fe9355410d41c62",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000168"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "第 11 章",
                "概率论预备知识"
              ],
              "lineStart": 9922,
              "lineEnd": 10003,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "9a0c45dc11fcad1719b50763f92c6e5e8671d5d5871170e328344fc4551433bf"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-binomial-scale",
        "moduleId": "random-variables",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "估计式给出的量级",
        "markdown": "当 $k$ 固定而 $n$ 增大时，下界说明 $\\binom{n}{k}$ 至少按 $n^{k}$ 的量级增长，上界给出同阶范围内的常数因子。分析随机算法时通常只需要这种量级结论，而不必求出组合数的精确数值。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "textbook-binomial-estimate"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "textbook-expectation",
        "moduleId": "expectation",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "期望与线性性质",
        "markdown": "随机变量的加权平均值称为期望，记作 $\\operatorname{E}[X]$。例如上面的二项分布随机变量有\n\n$$\\operatorname{E}[X]=\\sum_{i=0}^{n}i\\binom{n}{i}2^{-n}$$\n\n若 $X,Y$ 是同一概率空间上的随机变量，可以定义新的随机变量 $X+Y$ 与 $aX$。期望具有线性性质：\n\n$$\\operatorname{E}[aX+bY]=a\\operatorname{E}[X]+b\\operatorname{E}[Y]$$\n\n特别当 $X=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_i$ 时，有 $\\operatorname{E}[X]=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\operatorname{E}[X_i]$。以抛硬币为例，令 $X_i$ 表示第 $i$ 次抛掷的结果（正面为 1、反面为 0），则 $\\operatorname{E}[X_i]=1/2$，于是 $\\operatorname{E}[X]=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}1/2=n/2$。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-1806e31d4fe9355410d41c62",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000168"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "第 11 章",
                "概率论预备知识"
              ],
              "lineStart": 9922,
              "lineEnd": 10003,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "9a0c45dc11fcad1719b50763f92c6e5e8671d5d5871170e328344fc4551433bf"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-linearity-no-independence",
        "moduleId": "expectation",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "misconception",
        "title": "线性性不要求独立",
        "markdown": "常见误解：以为使用 $\\operatorname{E}[X+Y]=\\operatorname{E}[X]+\\operatorname{E}[Y]$ 必须先假定 $X$ 与 $Y$ 独立。实际上期望的线性性质对任意随机变量都成立，不需要任何独立性假设；独立性只在计算乘积的期望 $\\operatorname{E}[XY]$ 或合并方差时才需要额外条件。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "textbook-expectation"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "textbook-markov",
        "moduleId": "first-moment-bound",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "formula",
        "title": "马尔科夫不等式",
        "markdown": "对于取值非负的随机变量 $X$，一个有用的性质是\n\n$$\\Pr[X\\ge k\\operatorname{E}[X]]\\le\\frac{1}{k}$$\n\n或者写成 $\\Pr[X\\ge k]\\le\\operatorname{E}[X]/k$，这称为马尔科夫不等式。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-1806e31d4fe9355410d41c62",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000168"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "第 11 章",
